ValueSet: MimicMedicationStatementCode
Id: mimic-medication-statement-code
Title: "MIMIC MedicationStatement.medication[x] code"
Description: "The codes bound below MedicationStatement.medication[x] on MimicMedicationStatementED. Grouping ValueSet for CANONICAL IDENTITY ONLY — it is NEVER BOUND ANYWHERE, and the slice bindings in SD_MimicMedicationStatementED.fsh stay exactly as they are. MEMBERSHIP IS THE UNION OF THE TWO SLICE VALUESETS (mimic-medication-gsn, mimic-medication-etc) and no instance validates differently, because nothing validates against this ValueSet at all. It exists because every other map in the terminology-mapping pipeline names exactly one bound ValueSet as its sourceCanonical, and this element is the exception: the bindings sit on the coding slices, not on the CodeableConcept, so there are two bound ValueSets and no single canonical for a map to declare. Without a facade, MedicationStatement.medication[x] would either get no ConceptMap or get one that names only half the column — a $translate against mimic-medication-gsn alone would answer 'never observed' for every ETC code in medrecon, which is false. The facade must NOT replace the slice bindings: a slice-level required binding validates each coding against its own system, whereas binding this union at the CodeableConcept level would legalise a GSN code sitting in the etc slice (and, worse, a required CodeableConcept binding would pass whenever any one coding matched, while invalidating every row that carries only the mandatory free-text name — 11,708 resources, 0.45%, measured 2026-08-10; note FINDINGS.md D3's ~68% text-only figure does NOT hold for this element). The ndc slice deliberately stays unbound because no terminology server hosts http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/ndc (see scripts/binding-analysis/FINDINGS.md D3); NDC codings are therefore outside every bound enumeration by design, and outside this union too — they are not missing from it, they were never enumerable. Same device as mimic-medication-code and mimic-medication-request-code, and same union mechanic as mimic-medication-administration-merged-code, but for a different reason: those disambiguate elements or merge sub-types, this one gives a split-binding element a single canonical to be mapped by. Not part of the upstream MIMIC IG."

* include codes from valueset $GSN_VS
* include codes from valueset $ETC_VS
